  slide "AIPerf: in-process admission and dispatch" {
    eyebrow: "AIPerf architecture"
    title: "Admission and dispatch live inside one process"
    lede: "Admission, credit issuance, and observation stay inside the `--execute` process. `runtime.dispatch` selects how workers share a concurrency/rate gate (`sharded`, `global`, or `global-hop`). Optional cellular mode adds a controller that merges cell results over Velo control traffic — measured load rides HTTP or gRPC directly from each worker."

    narration: "Admission and dispatch are in-process. Cellular merge uses Velo for control only; measured load stays on HTTP or gRPC."

    term: {
      word: "dispatch mode"
      meaning: "How `workers > 1` admits and issues work inside one cell: `sharded` partitions budgets statically per thread, `global` admits concurrency and rate from a shared per-cell gate, and `global-hop` additionally routes every request through one coordinator-owned dispatcher for exact global issuance order. All three run inside one process."
    }

    points: [
      "Admission and credit issuance live in-process — workers draw work straight from a shared in-process gate.",
      "Each worker owns a LocalSet, transport sink, and local capture; metrics merge at phase boundaries.",
      "`dispatch` chooses sharded, global, or global-hop sharing of the concurrency/rate gate — still one process.",
      "Optional `--cells`: controller merges records or folded stores over Velo; inference traffic stays on HTTP or gRPC."
    ]

    caption: "In-process gates and sinks; cellular merge rides Velo control traffic."

    render: @scene {
      sdk.Header(
        id = "s6-hdr",
        title = "IN-PROCESS ADMISSION · DISPATCH",
        caption = "In-process gates and sinks; cellular merge rides Velo control traffic.",
